window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b229-9e0aa54b697fc1ac.json"]={sha256:"9e0aa54b697fc1ac2b1093e494cbc8dbb08487844d03037f7965ec51e7a6a568",value:{"id":"b229","title":"福爾柯克水輪","titleEn":"Falkirk Wheel","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以福爾柯克水輪為入口，深入旋轉升船的浮力平衡、齒輪定向與循環能量。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Falkirk Wheel as its entry point, this course examines buoyant balance, geared orientation and cycle energy in a rotating boat lift. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-lock","architectureNodes":[["成對船槽質量平衡","Paired gondola mass balance"],["船槽水平與齒輪定向","Gondola leveling by gearing"],["轉動慣量與加速","Rotational inertia and acceleration"],["螺栓預拉與接觸","Bolt pretension and joint contact"],["運河高差與分段提升","Canal elevation and staged lifting"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-lock","labels":["成對船槽質量平衡","船槽水平與齒輪定向","轉動慣量與加速","螺栓預拉與接觸","運河高差與分段提升"],"labelsEn":["Paired gondola mass balance","Gondola leveling by gearing","Rotational inertia and acceleration","Bolt pretension and joint contact","Canal elevation and staged lifting"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設每槽面積200 m²、其中一槽水位多0.02 m，淡水質量差4 t；若水平力臂12 m，最大重力轉矩Δmgr=470.88 kN·m。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設質量差3000 kg、半徑12 m、相對水平角60°，τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m；限集中質量與平面剛體。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 水位差敏感度固定槽面積200 m²、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²及水平力臂12 m，只將單槽多出的水深0.02 m減為0.01 m。Δm=ρAΔh由4 t降至2 t，重力轉矩ρAΔhgr由470.88降至235.44 kN·m。減半關係只適用此水平姿態的集中質量模型，不代表整圈轉動的實際電能或任意角度轉矩。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume gondola area 200 m² and one level higher by 0.02 m, giving freshwater imbalance 4 t. At horizontal lever arm 12 m, maximum gravity torque Δmgr=470.88 kN·m. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance 3000 kg, radius 12 m and angle sixty degrees above horizontal. τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m, for planar rigid motion with concentrated masses. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. Hold gondola area 200 m², ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s² and horizontal lever arm 12 m fixed, reducing only excess depth from 0.02 m to 0.01 m. Imbalance Δm=ρAΔh falls from 4 t to 2 t and gravity torque ρAΔhgr from 470.88 to 235.44 kN·m. Halving applies to this horizontal concentrated-mass model, not full-rotation electricity use or torque at every angle.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b229-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「成對船槽質量平衡」與「重力轉矩隨角度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Paired gondola mass balance\" and \"Gravity torque versus angle\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b229-v15-01","title":"成對船槽質量平衡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Paired gondola mass balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「成對船槽質量平衡」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Paired gondola mass balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水輪兩端船槽以近似相等總質量降低重力轉矩，浮船排出等重水是關鍵。但船槽水位差、積水和附著物仍會破壞理想對稱。 取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設每槽面積200 m²、其中一槽水位多0.02 m，淡水質量差4 t；若水平力臂12 m，最大重力轉矩Δmgr=470.88 kN·m。 船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。只看船舶重量而忽略水位，會把真正不平衡原因歸錯對象。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「成對船槽質量平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Paired gondolas reduce gravitational torque by maintaining nearly equal total masses, using equal-weight displacement by floating boats. Level differences, retained water and deposits can still break the ideal symmetry. Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume gondola area 200 m² and one level higher by 0.02 m, giving freshwater imbalance 4 t. At horizontal lever arm 12 m, maximum gravity torque Δmgr=470.88 kN·m. Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. Looking only at vessel mass while ignoring level misidentifies the source of the gravitational imbalance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Paired gondola mass balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「成對船槽質量平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Paired gondola mass balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-01-k1","title":"成對船槽質量平衡","titleEn":"Paired gondola mass balance","text":"水輪兩端船槽以近似相等總質量降低重力轉矩，浮船排出等重水是關鍵。但船槽水位差、積水和附著物仍會破壞理想對稱。","textEn":"Paired gondolas reduce gravitational torque by maintaining nearly equal total masses, using equal-weight displacement by floating boats. Level differences, retained water and deposits can still break the ideal symmetry.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「成對船槽質量平衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Paired gondola mass balance\" is correct?","options":["兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。","水輪兩端船槽以近似相等總質量降低重力轉矩，浮船排出等重水是關鍵。","質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。"],"optionsEn":["With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels.","Paired gondolas reduce gravitational torque by maintaining nearly equal total masses, using equal-weight displacement by floating boats.","A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水輪兩端船槽以近似相等總質量降低重力轉矩，浮船排出等重水是關鍵。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Paired gondolas reduce gravitational torque by maintaining nearly equal total masses, using equal-weight displacement by floating boats. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b229-v15-02","title":"成對船槽質量平衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Paired gondola mass balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「成對船槽質量平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Paired gondola mass balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設每槽面積200 m²、其中一槽水位多0.02 m，淡水質量差4 t；若水平力臂12 m，最大重力轉矩Δmgr=470.88 kN·m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume gondola area 200 m² and one level higher by 0.02 m, giving freshwater imbalance 4 t. At horizontal lever arm 12 m, maximum gravity torque Δmgr=470.88 kN·m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設每槽面積200 m²、其中一槽水位多0.02 m，淡水質量差4 t；若水平力臂12 m，最大重力轉矩Δmgr=470.88 kN·m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume gondola area 200 m² and one level higher by 0.02 m, giving freshwater imbalance 4 t. At horizontal lever arm 12 m, maximum gravity torque Δmgr=470.88 kN·m.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「成對船槽質量平衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Paired gondola mass balance\", which statement holds?","options":["半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。","設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant.","Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b229-v15-03","title":"成對船槽質量平衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Paired gondola mass balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「成對船槽質量平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Paired gondola mass balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。把多餘水量與兩槽質量差放在同一張平衡表。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Use opposite-direction torque differences to check imbalance and determine whether its maximum occurs near the horizontal position. Place excess water and the two-gondola mass difference in one balance sheet. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以成對船槽質量平衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for paired gondola mass balance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Use opposite-direction torque differences to check imbalance and determine whether its maximum occurs near the horizontal position.","failure":"注意干擾：船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。把多餘水量與兩槽質量差放在同一張平衡表。","textEn":"Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Use opposite-direction torque differences to check imbalance and determine whether its maximum occurs near the horizontal position. Place excess water and the two-gondola mass difference in one balance sheet.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以成對船槽質量平衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for paired gondola mass balance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Use opposite-direction torque differences to check imbalance and determine whether its maximum occurs near the horizontal position.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「成對船槽質量平衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Paired gondola mass balance\"?","options":["比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。"],"optionsEn":["Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較兩槽水位與總重推估，將浮船排水和多餘儲水分開；用正反向轉矩差核對不平衡來源，再檢查最大差值是否出現在水平位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare both levels and inferred mass, separating vessel displacement from excess stored water. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b229-v15-04","title":"成對船槽質量平衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Paired gondola mass balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「成對船槽質量平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Paired gondola mass balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。只看船舶重量而忽略水位，會把真正不平衡原因歸錯對象。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. Looking only at vessel mass while ignoring level misidentifies the source of the gravitational imbalance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只看船舶重量而忽略水位，會把真正不平衡原因歸錯對象。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Looking only at vessel mass while ignoring level misidentifies the source of the gravitational imbalance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。只看船舶重量而忽略水位，會把真正不平衡原因歸錯對象。","textEn":"Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. Looking only at vessel mass while ignoring level misidentifies the source of the gravitational imbalance.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「成對船槽質量平衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Paired gondola mass balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。","質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water.","A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"船舶自由浮動不代表船槽水位自動相同，排水路徑受阻時額外水量仍會增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Free flotation does not automatically equalize gondola levels, and obstructed drainage can retain extra water. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b229-v15-05","title":"重力轉矩隨角度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gravity torque versus angle: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「重力轉矩隨角度」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gravity torque versus angle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"質量差對旋轉軸的力臂隨角度改變，垂直位置重力轉矩可以接近零，水平位置則較大。固定轉矩模型無法描述整個半圈動作。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設質量差3000 kg、半徑12 m、相對水平角60°，τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m；限集中質量與平面剛體。 若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。傳動摩擦和風力也可能改變曲線，不能把所有殘差當成質量差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「重力轉矩隨角度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The lever arm of a mass imbalance changes with angle. Gravity torque can approach zero vertically and peak horizontally, so constant torque cannot describe an entire half-turn. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance 3000 kg, radius 12 m and angle sixty degrees above horizontal. τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m, for planar rigid motion with concentrated masses. Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. Friction and wind also alter the curve, so residuals do not uniquely reveal mass imbalance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gravity torque versus angle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「重力轉矩隨角度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gravity torque versus angle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-05-k1","title":"重力轉矩隨角度","titleEn":"Gravity torque versus angle","text":"質量差對旋轉軸的力臂隨角度改變，垂直位置重力轉矩可以接近零，水平位置則較大。固定轉矩模型無法描述整個半圈動作。","textEn":"The lever arm of a mass imbalance changes with angle. Gravity torque can approach zero vertically and peak horizontally, so constant torque cannot describe an entire half-turn.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「重力轉矩隨角度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gravity torque versus angle\" is correct?","options":["質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。","只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。","質量差對旋轉軸的力臂隨角度改變，垂直位置重力轉矩可以接近零，水平位置則較大。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.","A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.","The lever arm of a mass imbalance changes with angle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"質量差對旋轉軸的力臂隨角度改變，垂直位置重力轉矩可以接近零，水平位置則較大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The lever arm of a mass imbalance changes with angle. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b229-v15-06","title":"重力轉矩隨角度：定量估算","titleEn":"Gravity torque versus angle: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「重力轉矩隨角度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gravity torque versus angle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設質量差3000 kg、半徑12 m、相對水平角60°，τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m；限集中質量與平面剛體。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance 3000 kg, radius 12 m and angle sixty degrees above horizontal. τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m, for planar rigid motion with concentrated masses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設質量差3000 kg、半徑12 m、相對水平角60°，τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m；限集中質量與平面剛體。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance 3000 kg, radius 12 m and angle sixty degrees above horizontal. τ=Δmgrcosθ=176.58 kN·m, for planar rigid motion with concentrated masses.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「重力轉矩隨角度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gravity torque versus angle\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。","預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.","All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b229-v15-07","title":"重力轉矩隨角度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gravity torque versus angle: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「重力轉矩隨角度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gravity torque versus angle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。以水平與垂直位置的理論極值檢查角度定義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Use opposite rotation to distinguish friction sign and verify consistent angle zero and gravity direction. Use theoretical horizontal and vertical extrema to verify the chosen angular reference. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以重力轉矩隨角度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gravity torque versus angle, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Use opposite rotation to distinguish friction sign and verify consistent angle zero and gravity direction.","failure":"注意干擾：若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。以水平與垂直位置的理論極值檢查角度定義。","textEn":"Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Use opposite rotation to distinguish friction sign and verify consistent angle zero and gravity direction. Use theoretical horizontal and vertical extrema to verify the chosen angular reference.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以重力轉矩隨角度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gravity torque versus angle, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Use opposite rotation to distinguish friction sign and verify consistent angle zero and gravity direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「重力轉矩隨角度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gravity torque versus angle\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。","只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape.","A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將實測轉矩扣除慣性項後對轉角作圖，比較餘弦形狀；再以不同旋轉方向辨別摩擦符號，確認角度零點和重力方向一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot measured torque minus inertia against angle and compare the cosine shape. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b229-v15-08","title":"重力轉矩隨角度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gravity torque versus angle: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「重力轉矩隨角度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gravity torque versus angle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。傳動摩擦和風力也可能改變曲線，不能把所有殘差當成質量差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. Friction and wind also alter the curve, so residuals do not uniquely reveal mass imbalance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：傳動摩擦和風力也可能改變曲線，不能把所有殘差當成質量差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Friction and wind also alter the curve, so residuals do not uniquely reveal mass imbalance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。傳動摩擦和風力也可能改變曲線，不能把所有殘差當成質量差。","textEn":"Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. Friction and wind also alter the curve, so residuals do not uniquely reveal mass imbalance.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重力轉矩隨角度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gravity torque versus angle\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。","若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.","Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把角度從垂直量起卻沿用餘弦公式，轉矩峰值位置會錯九十度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using an angle measured from vertical in a horizontal-reference cosine shifts the predicted peak by ninety degrees. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b229-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「船槽水平與齒輪定向」與「旋轉速度與旅程」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gondola leveling by gearing\" and \"Rotation speed and travel\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b229-v15-09","title":"船槽水平與齒輪定向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gondola leveling by gearing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「船槽水平與齒輪定向」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gondola leveling by gearing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。這是運動學約束，不是只靠自由擺動就能保證的結果。 假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。 齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船槽水平與齒輪定向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. This is a kinematic constraint rather than a result guaranteed solely by free swinging. Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts. Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gondola leveling by gearing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gondola leveling by gearing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-09-k1","title":"船槽水平與齒輪定向","titleEn":"Gondola leveling by gearing","text":"船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。這是運動學約束，不是只靠自由擺動就能保證的結果。","textEn":"Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. This is a kinematic constraint rather than a result guaranteed solely by free swinging.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「船槽水平與齒輪定向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gondola leveling by gearing\" is correct?","options":["船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。","只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。","半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。"],"optionsEn":["Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground.","A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.","Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b229-v15-10","title":"船槽水平與齒輪定向：定量估算","titleEn":"Gondola leveling by gearing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gondola leveling by gearing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gondola leveling by gearing\", which statement holds?","options":["設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。","管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。"],"optionsEn":["Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it.","Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b229-v15-11","title":"船槽水平與齒輪定向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gondola leveling by gearing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「船槽水平與齒輪定向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gondola leveling by gearing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。另以獨立傾角計檢查水面與槽體的相對角度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Plot reversal backlash separately from structural bending instead of combining them into one orientation error. Use an independent inclinometer to compare water-surface orientation with gondola orientation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以船槽水平與齒輪定向編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gondola leveling by gearing, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Plot reversal backlash separately from structural bending instead of combining them into one orientation error.","failure":"注意干擾：齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。另以獨立傾角計檢查水面與槽體的相對角度。","textEn":"Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Plot reversal backlash separately from structural bending instead of combining them into one orientation error. Use an independent inclinometer to compare water-surface orientation with gondola orientation.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以船槽水平與齒輪定向編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for gondola leveling by gearing, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Plot reversal backlash separately from structural bending instead of combining them into one orientation error.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「船槽水平與齒輪定向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gondola leveling by gearing\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。","以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.","Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure arm and gondola angles against a ground-level reference and check their sum over the full travel. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b229-v15-12","title":"船槽水平與齒輪定向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gondola leveling by gearing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gondola leveling by gearing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。","textEn":"Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「船槽水平與齒輪定向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gondola leveling by gearing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。"],"optionsEn":["Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b229-v15-13","title":"旋轉速度與旅程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rotation speed and travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「旋轉速度與旅程」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rotation speed and travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"半圈旋轉的平均角速度與最大角速度不同，啟停段必須留出加減速。船槽線速度也隨半徑變化，不能把軸的轉速當成乘客的平移速度。 假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。 將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。若半徑取到錯誤位置，換算船槽邊緣速度也會系統性偏差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「旋轉速度與旅程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean half-turn angular speed differs from maximum speed because start and stop need acceleration. Gondola linear speed also depends on radius, so shaft rotation is not passenger translation speed. Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s. Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. A radius taken to the wrong point also systematically miscalculates speed at the gondola edge. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotation speed and travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「旋轉速度與旅程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rotation speed and travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-13-k1","title":"旋轉速度與旅程","titleEn":"Rotation speed and travel","text":"半圈旋轉的平均角速度與最大角速度不同，啟停段必須留出加減速。船槽線速度也隨半徑變化，不能把軸的轉速當成乘客的平移速度。","textEn":"Mean half-turn angular speed differs from maximum speed because start and stop need acceleration. Gondola linear speed also depends on radius, so shaft rotation is not passenger translation speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「旋轉速度與旅程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rotation speed and travel\" is correct?","options":["半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。","半圈旋轉的平均角速度與最大角速度不同，啟停段必須留出加減速。","兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。"],"optionsEn":["Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant.","Mean half-turn angular speed differs from maximum speed because start and stop need acceleration.","Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"半圈旋轉的平均角速度與最大角速度不同，啟停段必須留出加減速。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean half-turn angular speed differs from maximum speed because start and stop need acceleration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b229-v15-14","title":"旋轉速度與旅程：定量估算","titleEn":"Rotation speed and travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「旋轉速度與旅程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rotation speed and travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「旋轉速度與旅程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rotation speed and travel\", which statement holds?","options":["預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。","只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s。"],"optionsEn":["All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt.","A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設半圈轉動歷時300 s、勻速近似，ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s；半徑12 m的速度v=ωr=0.12566 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a half-turn over 300 s with uniform-speed approximation. ω=π/300=0.010472 rad/s and speed at radius 12 m is v=ωr=0.12566 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b229-v15-15","title":"旋轉速度與旅程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rotation speed and travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「旋轉速度與旅程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rotation speed and travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。同時計算不同半徑位置的線速度以檢查換算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Compare mean and peak values and ensure filtering has not erased brief changes in speed. Calculate linear speeds at several radii to check the geometric conversion independently. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以旋轉速度與旅程編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rotation speed and travel, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Compare mean and peak values and ensure filtering has not erased brief changes in speed.","failure":"注意干擾：將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。同時計算不同半徑位置的線速度以檢查換算。","textEn":"Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Compare mean and peak values and ensure filtering has not erased brief changes in speed. Calculate linear speeds at several radii to check the geometric conversion independently.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以旋轉速度與旅程編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rotation speed and travel, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Compare mean and peak values and ensure filtering has not erased brief changes in speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「旋轉速度與旅程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rotation speed and travel\"?","options":["從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從角位置歷線估算速度並核對線性位移，清楚標記加減速段；比較平均值與峰值，並確認資料濾波沒有把短時速度變化抹去。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate speed from angle history and verify it against linear travel, marking acceleration intervals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b229-v15-16","title":"旋轉速度與旅程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rotation speed and travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「旋轉速度與旅程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rotation speed and travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。若半徑取到錯誤位置，換算船槽邊緣速度也會系統性偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. A radius taken to the wrong point also systematically miscalculates speed at the gondola edge. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若半徑取到錯誤位置，換算船槽邊緣速度也會系統性偏差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A radius taken to the wrong point also systematically miscalculates speed at the gondola edge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。若半徑取到錯誤位置，換算船槽邊緣速度也會系統性偏差。","textEn":"Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. A radius taken to the wrong point also systematically miscalculates speed at the gondola edge.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「旋轉速度與旅程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rotation speed and travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。","兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing.","Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將全程平均速度當成處處相同會低估加速段需求，非均勻運轉亦影響水面晃蕩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using average speed everywhere misses acceleration demand, while nonuniform movement excites water sloshing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b229-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「轉動慣量與加速」與「整循環能量與損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rotational inertia and acceleration\" and \"Full-cycle energy and losses\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b229-v15-17","title":"轉動慣量與加速：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rotational inertia and acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「轉動慣量與加速」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rotational inertia and acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"質量平衡消除部分重力需求，卻不消除轉動慣量。遠離軸心的質量對慣量按半徑平方增加，因此外緣附加設備對啟停需求尤其敏感。 假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。 把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。若用靜態平衡證明馬達能力，便完全漏掉啟停時的動力需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉動慣量與加速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mass balance removes some gravity demand but not rotational inertia. Mass farther from the axis contributes with radius squared, making equipment added near the rim especially important during starting and stopping. Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m. I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²; angular acceleration 0.0002 rad/s² requires 14.4 kN·m, excluding wheel arms. A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. Static balance alone cannot establish motor capability because it omits starting and stopping demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotational inertia and acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「轉動慣量與加速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rotational inertia and acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-17-k1","title":"轉動慣量與加速","titleEn":"Rotational inertia and acceleration","text":"質量平衡消除部分重力需求，卻不消除轉動慣量。遠離軸心的質量對慣量按半徑平方增加，因此外緣附加設備對啟停需求尤其敏感。","textEn":"Mass balance removes some gravity demand but not rotational inertia. Mass farther from the axis contributes with radius squared, making equipment added near the rim especially important during starting and stopping.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉動慣量與加速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rotational inertia and acceleration\" is correct?","options":["兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。","設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","質量平衡消除部分重力需求，卻不消除轉動慣量。"],"optionsEn":["Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.","Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","Mass balance removes some gravity demand but not rotational inertia."],"answer":2,"explanation":"質量平衡消除部分重力需求，卻不消除轉動慣量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mass balance removes some gravity demand but not rotational inertia. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b229-v15-18","title":"轉動慣量與加速：定量估算","titleEn":"Rotational inertia and acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「轉動慣量與加速」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rotational inertia and acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m. I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²; angular acceleration 0.0002 rad/s² requires 14.4 kN·m, excluding wheel arms. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m. I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²; angular acceleration 0.0002 rad/s² requires 14.4 kN·m, excluding wheel arms.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「轉動慣量與加速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rotational inertia and acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²。","管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。","官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m.","Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling.","The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩槽各250000 kg、集中於半徑12 m，I=2mr²=72 million kg·m²；角加速度0.0002 rad/s²需14.4 kN·m，未含輪臂。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two gondolas each 250000 kg concentrated at radius 12 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b229-v15-19","title":"轉動慣量與加速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rotational inertia and acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「轉動慣量與加速」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rotational inertia and acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。用動能變化率交叉核對加速段的機械功率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Compare acceleration torque after subtracting gravity and friction, checking for omitted rotating components. Cross-check acceleration-phase mechanical power against the rate of kinetic-energy change. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以轉動慣量與加速編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rotational inertia and acceleration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Compare acceleration torque after subtracting gravity and friction, checking for omitted rotating components.","failure":"注意干擾：把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。用動能變化率交叉核對加速段的機械功率。","textEn":"Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Compare acceleration torque after subtracting gravity and friction, checking for omitted rotating components. Cross-check acceleration-phase mechanical power against the rate of kinetic-energy change.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以轉動慣量與加速編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rotational inertia and acceleration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Compare acceleration torque after subtracting gravity and friction, checking for omitted rotating components.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「轉動慣量與加速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rotational inertia and acceleration\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。","質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions.","A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按實際質量分布建立慣量清單，核對槽、輪臂、傳動與附加設備；以加速段轉矩扣除重力和摩擦後比較，檢查是否遺漏旋轉件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Create an inertia inventory from actual mass distribution, including gondolas, arms, drivetrain and additions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b229-v15-20","title":"轉動慣量與加速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rotational inertia and acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「轉動慣量與加速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rotational inertia and acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。若用靜態平衡證明馬達能力，便完全漏掉啟停時的動力需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. Static balance alone cannot establish motor capability because it omits starting and stopping demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若用靜態平衡證明馬達能力，便完全漏掉啟停時的動力需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Static balance alone cannot establish motor capability because it omits starting and stopping demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。若用靜態平衡證明馬達能力，便完全漏掉啟停時的動力需求。","textEn":"A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. Static balance alone cannot establish motor capability because it omits starting and stopping demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「轉動慣量與加速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rotational inertia and acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把全部質量放在單一半徑只是簡化，輪臂分布和傳動反射慣量可能不可忽略。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A single-radius mass representation is approximate; distributed arms and reflected drivetrain inertia may matter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b229-v15-21","title":"整循環能量與損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Full-cycle energy and losses: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「整循環能量與損失」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Full-cycle energy and losses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想成對升降可互相交換位能，實際電力主要補足損失和不平衡。整循環比較須包括正負功率與輔助設備，不能用某一瞬間功率乘任意時間。 假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。 忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。宣傳用水壺類比缺乏共同容量時，不能替代電表紀錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「整循環能量與損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ideal paired motion exchanges potential energy, while electricity covers losses and imbalance. A cycle balance includes positive and negative power and auxiliaries rather than multiplying one instantaneous reading by an arbitrary duration. Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s. Total energy is (18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh, not official energy use. Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. Kettle analogies without common capacity and duration cannot replace metered energy records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Full-cycle energy and losses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「整循環能量與損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Full-cycle energy and losses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-21-k1","title":"整循環能量與損失","titleEn":"Full-cycle energy and losses","text":"理想成對升降可互相交換位能，實際電力主要補足損失和不平衡。整循環比較須包括正負功率與輔助設備，不能用某一瞬間功率乘任意時間。","textEn":"Ideal paired motion exchanges potential energy, while electricity covers losses and imbalance. A cycle balance includes positive and negative power and auxiliaries rather than multiplying one instantaneous reading by an arbitrary duration.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「整循環能量與損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Full-cycle energy and losses\" is correct?","options":["理想成對升降可互相交換位能，實際電力主要補足損失和不平衡。","設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。"],"optionsEn":["Ideal paired motion exchanges potential energy, while electricity covers losses and imbalance.","Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt."],"answer":0,"explanation":"理想成對升降可互相交換位能，實際電力主要補足損失和不平衡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ideal paired motion exchanges potential energy, while electricity covers losses and imbalance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b229-v15-22","title":"整循環能量與損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Full-cycle energy and losses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「整循環能量與損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Full-cycle energy and losses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s. Total energy is (18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh, not official energy use. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s. Total energy is (18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh, not official energy use.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「整循環能量與損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Full-cycle energy and losses\", which statement holds?","options":["只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh。","兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。"],"optionsEn":["A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s.","With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設平均主驅動功率18 kW持續300 s，另輔助4 kW持續600 s，總能量=(18×300+4×600)/3600=2.1667 kWh；非官方耗能。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume main drive averages 18 kW for 300 s and auxiliaries 4 kW for 600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b229-v15-23","title":"整循環能量與損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Full-cycle energy and losses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「整循環能量與損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Full-cycle energy and losses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。核對循環起點與終點是否具有相同儲能狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Compare cycles at matched levels, weather and vessel conditions rather than ranking values with different energy boundaries. Check that cycle start and finish have equivalent stored-energy states. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以整循環能量與損失編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for full-cycle energy and losses, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Compare cycles at matched levels, weather and vessel conditions rather than ranking values with different energy boundaries.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。核對循環起點與終點是否具有相同儲能狀態。","textEn":"Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Compare cycles at matched levels, weather and vessel conditions rather than ranking values with different energy boundaries. Check that cycle start and finish have equivalent stored-energy states.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以整循環能量與損失編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for full-cycle energy and losses, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Compare cycles at matched levels, weather and vessel conditions rather than ranking values with different energy boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「整循環能量與損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Full-cycle energy and losses\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。","積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.","Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"積分完整循環的雙向電功率，清楚標示電表是否包含輔機和待機；比較相同水位、天候與船型條件的循環，避免不同邊界的數值相互排名。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate bidirectional power over a complete cycle and identify auxiliary and standby coverage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b229-v15-24","title":"整循環能量與損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Full-cycle energy and losses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「整循環能量與損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Full-cycle energy and losses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。宣傳用水壺類比缺乏共同容量時，不能替代電表紀錄。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. Kettle analogies without common capacity and duration cannot replace metered energy records. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：宣傳用水壺類比缺乏共同容量時，不能替代電表紀錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Kettle analogies without common capacity and duration cannot replace metered energy records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。宣傳用水壺類比缺乏共同容量時，不能替代電表紀錄。","textEn":"Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. Kettle analogies without common capacity and duration cannot replace metered energy records.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「整循環能量與損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Full-cycle energy and losses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略待機與門控能耗會低估每次服務能源，將回生能量在不同邊界重複扣除也會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting standby and gate-control loads understates service energy, while subtracting regeneration twice distorts the balance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b229-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「螺栓預拉與接觸」與「管形輪臂局部剛度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bolt pretension and joint contact\" and \"Tubular-arm section stiffness\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b229-v15-25","title":"螺栓預拉與接觸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bolt pretension and joint contact: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「螺栓預拉與接觸」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bolt pretension and joint contact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"輪臂連接的螺栓預拉力保持接觸並影響疲勞應力範圍，外力並非全部直接加到螺栓上。接頭剛度決定螺栓與被夾件的載荷分配。 假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。 表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。若把全部外力忽略或全部加到螺栓，都會誤判疲勞需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「螺栓預拉與接觸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pretension maintains contact and affects bolt fatigue range. Applied load does not all go directly into the bolt because relative bolt and clamped-part stiffness controls sharing. Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN. Before separation bolt force becomes 320 kN and clamping force falls by 80 kN. Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. Either ignoring applied load or adding it entirely to bolts misstates fatigue demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bolt pretension and joint contact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「螺栓預拉與接觸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bolt pretension and joint contact”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-25-k1","title":"螺栓預拉與接觸","titleEn":"Bolt pretension and joint contact","text":"輪臂連接的螺栓預拉力保持接觸並影響疲勞應力範圍，外力並非全部直接加到螺栓上。接頭剛度決定螺栓與被夾件的載荷分配。","textEn":"Pretension maintains contact and affects bolt fatigue range. Applied load does not all go directly into the bolt because relative bolt and clamped-part stiffness controls sharing.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「螺栓預拉與接觸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bolt pretension and joint contact\" is correct?","options":["預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。","輪臂連接的螺栓預拉力保持接觸並影響疲勞應力範圍，外力並非全部直接加到螺栓上。","管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。"],"optionsEn":["All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt.","Pretension maintains contact and affects bolt fatigue range.","Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輪臂連接的螺栓預拉力保持接觸並影響疲勞應力範圍，外力並非全部直接加到螺栓上。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pretension maintains contact and affects bolt fatigue range. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b229-v15-26","title":"螺栓預拉與接觸：定量估算","titleEn":"Bolt pretension and joint contact: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「螺栓預拉與接觸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bolt pretension and joint contact” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN. Before separation bolt force becomes 320 kN and clamping force falls by 80 kN. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN. Before separation bolt force becomes 320 kN and clamping force falls by 80 kN.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「螺栓預拉與接觸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bolt pretension and joint contact\", which statement holds?","options":["官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。","質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。"],"optionsEn":["The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.","A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設單螺栓預拉300 kN、接頭剛度分配係數0.2、外拉力100 kN，未分離時螺栓力320 kN、夾緊力減少80 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume bolt pretension 300 kN, stiffness fraction 0.2 and applied tension 100 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b229-v15-27","title":"螺栓預拉與接觸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bolt pretension and joint contact: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「螺栓預拉與接觸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bolt pretension and joint contact” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。將預拉損失與表面壓陷量作獨立相關比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Compare cyclic bolt strain with the predicted stiffness sharing under the applied loading cycle. Independently compare pretension loss with measured embedment of the contact surfaces. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以螺栓預拉與接觸編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for bolt pretension and joint contact, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Compare cyclic bolt strain with the predicted stiffness sharing under the applied loading cycle.","failure":"注意干擾：表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。將預拉損失與表面壓陷量作獨立相關比較。","textEn":"Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Compare cyclic bolt strain with the predicted stiffness sharing under the applied loading cycle. Independently compare pretension loss with measured embedment of the contact surfaces.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以螺栓預拉與接觸編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for bolt pretension and joint contact, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Compare cyclic bolt strain with the predicted stiffness sharing under the applied loading cycle.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「螺栓預拉與接觸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bolt pretension and joint contact\"?","options":["用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。"],"optionsEn":["Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用校準方法核對預拉而非只讀扳手扭矩，查接觸面是否分離或滑移；將外載循環造成的螺栓應變幅與剛度分配模型交叉比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify pretension with a calibrated method rather than torque alone, checking separation and slip. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b229-v15-28","title":"螺栓預拉與接觸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bolt pretension and joint contact: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「螺栓預拉與接觸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bolt pretension and joint contact” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。若把全部外力忽略或全部加到螺栓，都會誤判疲勞需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. Either ignoring applied load or adding it entirely to bolts misstates fatigue demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把全部外力忽略或全部加到螺栓，都會誤判疲勞需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Either ignoring applied load or adding it entirely to bolts misstates fatigue demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。若把全部外力忽略或全部加到螺栓，都會誤判疲勞需求。","textEn":"Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. Either ignoring applied load or adding it entirely to bolts misstates fatigue demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「螺栓預拉與接觸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bolt pretension and joint contact\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。","管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing.","Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面嵌入和鬆弛可能降低夾緊力而扭矩標記仍在，接頭分離後線性分配失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Embedment and relaxation can reduce clamp force despite intact torque marks, and separation invalidates linear sharing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b229-v15-29","title":"管形輪臂局部剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tubular-arm section stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「管形輪臂局部剛度」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tubular-arm section stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管形截面把材料移到外側提高彎曲剛度，但薄壁局部屈曲和焊接細節仍可能控制。截面慣性矩只描述整體彎曲，不能取代局部板件分析。 假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。 局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。平均厚度無法代表腐蝕坑或焊趾附近的局部承載，不能只以整體撓度驗收。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「管形輪臂局部剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tubular sections place material outward to increase bending stiffness, but local shell buckling and welded details can govern. Section inertia describes overall bending rather than local wall behavior. Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m. I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴, for an intact uniform tube without openings or local thinning. A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. Mean thickness misses pits and local weld-toe demands, so global deflection alone cannot establish local adequacy. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tubular-arm section stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「管形輪臂局部剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tubular-arm section stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-29-k1","title":"管形輪臂局部剛度","titleEn":"Tubular-arm section stiffness","text":"管形截面把材料移到外側提高彎曲剛度，但薄壁局部屈曲和焊接細節仍可能控制。截面慣性矩只描述整體彎曲，不能取代局部板件分析。","textEn":"Tubular sections place material outward to increase bending stiffness, but local shell buckling and welded details can govern. Section inertia describes overall bending rather than local wall behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「管形輪臂局部剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tubular-arm section stiffness\" is correct?","options":["管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。","只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。","管形截面把材料移到外側提高彎曲剛度，但薄壁局部屈曲和焊接細節仍可能控制。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling.","A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.","Tubular sections place material outward to increase bending stiffness, but local shell buckling and welded details can govern."],"answer":2,"explanation":"管形截面把材料移到外側提高彎曲剛度，但薄壁局部屈曲和焊接細節仍可能控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tubular sections place material outward to increase bending stiffness, but local shell buckling and welded details can govern. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b229-v15-30","title":"管形輪臂局部剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Tubular-arm section stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「管形輪臂局部剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tubular-arm section stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m. I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴, for an intact uniform tube without openings or local thinning. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m. I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴, for an intact uniform tube without openings or local thinning.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「管形輪臂局部剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tubular-arm section stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。","兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。","只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m.","With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels.","A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設圓管外徑1 m、內徑0.9 m，I=π(D⁴−d⁴)/64=0.01688 m⁴；均勻完整圓管，不含開孔和局部薄化。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume circular tube outer diameter 1 m and inner diameter 0.9 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b229-v15-31","title":"管形輪臂局部剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tubular-arm section stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「管形輪臂局部剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tubular-arm section stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。對最薄壁段另行檢查局部曲率與凹陷深度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Use multiple strains to test linear bending assumptions and inspect local dents separately from overall member curvature. Inspect local curvature and dent depth separately in the thinnest wall regions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以管形輪臂局部剛度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for tubular-arm section stiffness, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Use multiple strains to test linear bending assumptions and inspect local dents separately from overall member curvature.","failure":"注意干擾：局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。對最薄壁段另行檢查局部曲率與凹陷深度。","textEn":"Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Use multiple strains to test linear bending assumptions and inspect local dents separately from overall member curvature. Inspect local curvature and dent depth separately in the thinnest wall regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以管形輪臂局部剛度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for tubular-arm section stiffness, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Use multiple strains to test linear bending assumptions and inspect local dents separately from overall member curvature.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「管形輪臂局部剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tubular-arm section stiffness\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。","兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations.","Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對截面幾何與測厚分布，將開孔、加勁和焊縫位置納入模型；用多點應變檢查線性彎曲分布是否足夠，另查局部凹陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check geometry and thickness distribution, including openings, stiffeners and weld locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b229-v15-32","title":"管形輪臂局部剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tubular-arm section stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「管形輪臂局部剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tubular-arm section stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。平均厚度無法代表腐蝕坑或焊趾附近的局部承載，不能只以整體撓度驗收。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. Mean thickness misses pits and local weld-toe demands, so global deflection alone cannot establish local adequacy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均厚度無法代表腐蝕坑或焊趾附近的局部承載，不能只以整體撓度驗收。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean thickness misses pits and local weld-toe demands, so global deflection alone cannot establish local adequacy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管形截面整體慣性矩足夠就能排除所有局部屈曲。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate tubular section inertia rules out every form of local buckling.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。平均厚度無法代表腐蝕坑或焊趾附近的局部承載，不能只以整體撓度驗收。","textEn":"A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. Mean thickness misses pits and local weld-toe demands, so global deflection alone cannot establish local adequacy.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管形輪臂局部剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tubular-arm section stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。","局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.","A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部凹陷可能觸發薄壁失穩，即使全截面慣性矩幾乎不變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A local dent can trigger shell instability with little change in overall inertia. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b229-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「水面晃蕩時間尺度」與「運河高差與分段提升」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Free-surface sloshing time scale\" and \"Canal elevation and staged lifting\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b229-v15-33","title":"水面晃蕩時間尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Free-surface sloshing time scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「水面晃蕩時間尺度」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free-surface sloshing time scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。小振幅理論可比較尺度，實際船體和隔板會改變流場。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設矩形槽長20 m、水深2 m，k=π/L，ω²=gk tanh(kh)，第一模態T=2π/ω=9.177 s；無船且小振幅。 船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水面晃蕩時間尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length. Small-amplitude theory compares scales, while vessels and baffles modify the real flow. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume rectangular tank length 20 m and depth 2 m, with k=π/L and ω²=gk tanh(kh). First-mode T=2π/ω=9.177 s, for small motion without a vessel. A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Free-surface sloshing time scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水面晃蕩時間尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Free-surface sloshing time scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-33-k1","title":"水面晃蕩時間尺度","titleEn":"Free-surface sloshing time scale","text":"船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。小振幅理論可比較尺度，實際船體和隔板會改變流場。","textEn":"Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length. Small-amplitude theory compares scales, while vessels and baffles modify the real flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水面晃蕩時間尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Free-surface sloshing time scale\" is correct?","options":["船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。","只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。","官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。"],"optionsEn":["Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length.","A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.","The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b229-v15-34","title":"水面晃蕩時間尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Free-surface sloshing time scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水面晃蕩時間尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free-surface sloshing time scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設矩形槽長20 m、水深2 m，k=π/L，ω²=gk tanh(kh)，第一模態T=2π/ω=9.177 s；無船且小振幅。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume rectangular tank length 20 m and depth 2 m, with k=π/L and ω²=gk tanh(kh). First-mode T=2π/ω=9.177 s, for small motion without a vessel. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設矩形槽長20 m、水深2 m，k=π/L，ω²=gk tanh(kh)，第一模態T=2π/ω=9.177 s；無船且小振幅。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume rectangular tank length 20 m and depth 2 m, with k=π/L and ω²=gk tanh(kh). First-mode T=2π/ω=9.177 s, for small motion without a vessel.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水面晃蕩時間尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Free-surface sloshing time scale\", which statement holds?","options":["質量差固定時，整個旋轉過程的重力轉矩也固定。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","半圈平均角速度就是所有時刻的實際角速度。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed mass imbalance creates constant gravity torque throughout rotation.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","Half-turn mean angular speed equals the actual speed at every instant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b229-v15-35","title":"水面晃蕩時間尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Free-surface sloshing time scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水面晃蕩時間尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free-surface sloshing time scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。將船體存在與否對應不同的有效自由液面形狀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Validate occupied and empty conditions separately, preserving sensor saturation and splash intervals in the record. Relate vessel presence to the resulting change in effective free-surface geometry. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以水面晃蕩時間尺度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for free-surface sloshing time scale, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Validate occupied and empty conditions separately, preserving sensor saturation and splash intervals in the record.","failure":"注意干擾：船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。將船體存在與否對應不同的有效自由液面形狀。","textEn":"Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Validate occupied and empty conditions separately, preserving sensor saturation and splash intervals in the record. Relate vessel presence to the resulting change in effective free-surface geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以水面晃蕩時間尺度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for free-surface sloshing time scale, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Validate occupied and empty conditions separately, preserving sensor saturation and splash intervals in the record.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水面晃蕩時間尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Free-surface sloshing time scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設備保持重力平衡就保證整個服務循環完全不耗電。","比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Gravitational balance guarantees zero electrical use over the complete service cycle.","Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較槽內不同位置水位相位與船槽加速度頻譜，辨認駐波節點；用有船和無船資料分開驗證，並保留感測器飽和或濺水段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare level phase at several positions with gondola-acceleration spectra and identify standing-wave nodes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b229-v15-36","title":"水面晃蕩時間尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Free-surface sloshing time scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水面晃蕩時間尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free-surface sloshing time scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A central level sensor reliably captures every maximum sloshing response.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。","textEn":"A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水面晃蕩時間尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Free-surface sloshing time scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。"],"optionsEn":["A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b229-v15-37","title":"運河高差與分段提升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Canal elevation and staged lifting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「運河高差與分段提升」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Canal elevation and staged lifting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"整個運河連接高差可以由水輪與其他船閘共同完成，不能把整體高差全歸給單一設備。分段能量與水量盤點需要明確界定每個控制體。 假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。 把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。即使單一設備運轉正常，全航路仍可能受到其他節點限制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「運河高差與分段提升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A canal-level difference can be shared between a wheel and additional locks. Assigning the entire difference to one device misstates geometry; staged energy and water accounting requires clear control boundaries. Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities. Only 35 m is official canal context; 24 m is a teaching assumption. Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. A functioning wheel does not establish availability of the whole route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Canal elevation and staged lifting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities.","failure":"常見誤解：「官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「運河高差與分段提升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Canal elevation and staged lifting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-37-k1","title":"運河高差與分段提升","titleEn":"Canal elevation and staged lifting","text":"整個運河連接高差可以由水輪與其他船閘共同完成，不能把整體高差全歸給單一設備。分段能量與水量盤點需要明確界定每個控制體。","textEn":"A canal-level difference can be shared between a wheel and additional locks. Assigning the entire difference to one device misstates geometry; staged energy and water accounting requires clear control boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「運河高差與分段提升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Canal elevation and staged lifting\" is correct?","options":["官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。","整個運河連接高差可以由水輪與其他船閘共同完成，不能把整體高差全歸給單一設備。","兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。"],"optionsEn":["The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.","A canal-level difference can be shared between a wheel and additional locks.","With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"整個運河連接高差可以由水輪與其他船閘共同完成，不能把整體高差全歸給單一設備。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A canal-level difference can be shared between a wheel and additional locks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b229-v15-38","title":"運河高差與分段提升：定量估算","titleEn":"Canal elevation and staged lifting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「運河高差與分段提升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Canal elevation and staged lifting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities. Only 35 m is official canal context; 24 m is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities. Only 35 m is official canal context; 24 m is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「運河高差與分段提升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Canal elevation and staged lifting\", which statement holds?","options":["只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。","兩端質量完全平衡就代表旋轉慣量等於零。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。"],"optionsEn":["A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.","Perfectly balanced end masses make rotational inertia equal to zero.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設全線高差35 m、水輪部分24 m，其他設施需補11 m；這是分段算例，僅35 m採官方運河背景，24 m為教學假設。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total route difference 35 m and wheel portion 24 m, leaving 11 m for other facilities. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b229-v15-39","title":"運河高差與分段提升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Canal elevation and staged lifting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「運河高差與分段提升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Canal elevation and staged lifting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。逐段核對高程差總和是否回到兩運河實測差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Check definitions of advertised height, structural height and actual lift before using them interchangeably. Check that the sum of stage differences closes against the measured canal-level difference. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以運河高差與分段提升編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for canal elevation and staged lifting, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Check definitions of advertised height, structural height and actual lift before using them interchangeably.","failure":"注意干擾：把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。逐段核對高程差總和是否回到兩運河實測差。","textEn":"Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Check definitions of advertised height, structural height and actual lift before using them interchangeably. Check that the sum of stage differences closes against the measured canal-level difference.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以運河高差與分段提升編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for canal elevation and staged lifting, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Check definitions of advertised height, structural height and actual lift before using them interchangeably.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「運河高差與分段提升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Canal elevation and staged lifting\"?","options":["沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","預拉螺栓承受外拉力時，外力必定全部加到螺栓上。"],"optionsEn":["Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","All external tension must be added directly to every preloaded bolt."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿完整航路建立同基準縱剖面，逐一標出水輪、船閘與渠道水面；檢查宣傳高度、結構高度和實際提升高度的定義，避免相互替代。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a common-datum profile along the complete route, marking wheel, locks and reach levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b229-v15-40","title":"運河高差與分段提升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Canal elevation and staged lifting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b229-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「運河高差與分段提升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Canal elevation and staged lifting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。即使單一設備運轉正常，全航路仍可能受到其他節點限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. A functioning wheel does not establish availability of the whole route. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：即使單一設備運轉正常，全航路仍可能受到其他節點限制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A functioning wheel does not establish availability of the whole route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「官方運河總高差就是水輪單獨完成的精確提升高度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The official total canal difference is precisely the lift performed by the wheel alone.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b229-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。即使單一設備運轉正常，全航路仍可能受到其他節點限制。","textEn":"Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. A functioning wheel does not establish availability of the whole route.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b229-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「運河高差與分段提升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Canal elevation and staged lifting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。","兩端都有浮船時，不論水位如何都必定完全平衡。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use.","With floating boats on both ends the wheel is perfectly balanced at any levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把景觀總高度當提升高度會誇大能量需求，漏掉上游船閘又會低估通行時間與用水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using overall architectural height as lift exaggerates energy demand, while omitting upper locks understates transit time and water use. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-sc-wheel","v15s-sc-carbon","v15s-sc-location","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
